Description: st/mesa: only expose ASTC sliced 3D when 3D textures work
 KHR_texture_compression_astc_sliced_3d was enabled together with
 KHR_texture_compression_astc_ldr from 2D support of the ASTC formats. When
 the formats are supported natively in 2D, st does not emulate them:
 st_astc_format_fallback() decides from 2D sampler support of ASTC 4x4 and
 5x5 sRGB (has_astc_2d_ldr, has_astc_5x5_ldr), not per format and not per
 target. A TEXTURE_3D texture of such a format then needs native 3D support.
 Without it the extension allowed glCompressedTexImage3D(GL_TEXTURE_3D) with
 ASTC and the texture could not be created. Before the driver supported
 ASTC, the same textures were decoded in software and worked.
 .
 Disable the sliced 3D extension if an ASTC format with 2D blocks is supported
 for 2D sampling but not for PIPE_TEXTURE_3D. Fully emulated ASTC keeps it.
 With the extension off, TEXTURE_3D is rejected for ASTC as the
 KHR_texture_compression_astc_ldr specification requires.
 .
 This needs "zink: check 3D image support in is_format_supported" (patch 0079
 in this series), otherwise zink reports 3D support from the format features.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
